; Vendored Fmt (see README.md). `upstream/` is a git submodule pinned at the
; `v0.11.0` tag; the enclosing asm/dune marks this tree `vendored_dirs`, which
; suppresses warnings here and leaves it out of `@fmt`, so the copy stays
; verifiable against the pinned submodule commit.
;
; The vendored copy is what makes Fmt usable here at all: the opam `fmt`
; package is built by topkg and installs a META template, which dune rejects
; for Melange ("not compatible with melange support"), so the production
; closure could not depend on it and still satisfy .ai/asm_plan.md §11.6.
;
; Melange mode lives in melange/vendor/fmt, which copy_files these same
; sources.
;
; `data_only_dirs` keeps upstream/'s own build files (B0.ml, pkg/, _tags) out
; of dune's view. Fmt 0.11.0 ships no dune files of its own, so nothing
; upstream currently depends on this - but err_trace next door shows exactly
; what goes wrong the day a vendored submodule's own build machinery is left
; readable, so the same protection is applied here on principle.
(data_only_dirs upstream)

(copy_files#
 (files upstream/src/fmt.ml))

(copy_files#
 (files upstream/src/fmt.mli))

(library
 (name fmt)
 (modes byte native)
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{env:ASM_MELANGE=false} true)))
